From 8a7ec5d767fa3027e2bd4ad278c18b05fc6c8bed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:50:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban gc test: the scratch refusal memo loader
 drops a bool last_at/retry_at

Post-merge mutation check of #2448 (card t_01a1d61dee8aa5aa) found that
removing `and not isinstance(value, bool)` from `_finite` in
hermes_cli/kanban_scratch_backoff.py survived the suite: the parametrized
malformed-field test covered `{"count": True}` but no bool epoch. Under that
mutant a memo entry with `"last_at": true` or `"retry_at": true` loads as
well-formed, keeps its count for the next record() and skips the
"dropped N malformed" warning.

Adds `{"retry_at": True}` and `{"last_at": True}` to
test_memo_loader_drops_each_malformed_field. Test-only.

Proof (scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py):
- RED with the mutant: 2 failed (bad13 retry_at=True, bad14 last_at=True).
- GREEN at origin/main 800df5e171 + this test: 27 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py
index 6872e48608..3d0d4d6ccf 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_scratch_gc_backoff.py
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@ def test_malformed_memo_entry_is_dropped_and_the_aged_pass_completes(remote, arc
     {"last_at": "y"}, {"retry_at": float("inf")}, {"retry_at": 1e300}, {"retry_at": None},
     {"fingerprint": "p"}, {"reason": 5}, {"count": 10**10},
     {"retry_at": 9.9e10},  # below 1e11 but past Windows' gmtime limit (~year 3000)
+    {"retry_at": True}, {"last_at": True},  # bool is an int subclass, never an epoch
 ])
 def test_memo_loader_drops_each_malformed_field(tmp_path, bad):
     tree = tmp_path / "tree"
